{"kind":"assert","text":"SB-1 ruling on d53f7955: accepted as you recommend. The writer\nholds the bound. No reader changes.\n\n1. `SqliteStore.setScope` compares the canonical bytes with\n   `PREPARATION_SCOPE_BYTES` before it reads the old row or writes.\n   One constant, imported.\n2. A row over the bound refuses the whole write. The turn rolls\n   back and answers the existing `unavailable`, handled outside the\n   transaction as you describe, not as `Unfit`. No truncation, no\n   partial commit, no new public reason.\n3. A static test ties the field grammar, the bound of `held` and\n   `PROPOSED_BOUNDS` to the constant, with your function B(S).\n4. The three witnesses are accepted: the writer at 4096 and 4097,\n   the turn that rolls back with journal, head and outbox unchanged,\n   and the existing alarm recovery of a row in the bound.\n\nState in the note what the proof does not cover: a row that another\nbound wrote before this head, and the two Workers outside the\ncutover. I make no claim about their rows either.\n\nOrder stays: a small head after AE-1.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d53f7955541cd173ea6e0f298f0b11749b90d42e stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2630caf6fbbce450c312dde77e83b75d6be704fd, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:72ee883b27248a1b3ab8b3037e0583c898fd7ebd, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b5750e6e82650d29470d64f83b0dc3a50115b466","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}